{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 12,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.09,
            0.615,
            0.122
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "E X E R C I S E S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.139,
            0.896,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": "**1. Which of the following correctly describes the magnetic field near a long straight wire?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.177,
            0.754,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "**(a) The field consists of straight lines perpendicular to the wire.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.197,
            0.703,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "**(b) The field consists of straight lines parallel to the wire.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.217,
            0.734,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "**(c) The field consists of radial lines originating from the wire.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.238,
            0.737,
            0.258
          ],
          "content": "**(d) The field consists of concentric circles centred on the wire.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.258,
            0.644,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": "**2. At the time of short circuit, the current in the circuit**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.279,
            0.429,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "**(a) reduces substantially.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.3,
            0.383,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**(b) does not change.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.32,
            0.388,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "**(c) increases heavily.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.34,
            0.399,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "**(d) vary continuously.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.361,
            0.671,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": "**3. State whether the following statements are true or false.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.381,
            0.895,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": "**(a) The field at the centre of a long circular coil carrying current will be parallel straight lines.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.417,
            0.881,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "**(b) A wire with a green insulation is usually the live wire of an electric supply.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.441,
            0.595,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": "**4. List two methods of producing magnetic fields.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.462,
            0.895,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "**5. When is the force experienced by a current–carrying conductor placed in a magnetic field largest?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.498,
            0.896,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": "**6. Imagine that you are sitting in a chamber with your back to one wall. An electron beam, moving horizontally from back wall towards the front wall, is deflected by a strong magnetic field to your right side. What is the direction of magnetic field?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.55,
            0.896,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": "**7. State the rule to determine the direction of a (i) magnetic field produced around a straight conductor-carrying current, (ii) force experienced by a current-carrying straight conductor placed in a magnetic field which is perpendicular to it, and (iii) current induced in a coil due to its rotation in a magnetic field.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.618,
            0.556,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "**8. When does an electric short circuit occur?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.638,
            0.895,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": "**9. What is the function of an earth wire? Why is it necessary to earth metallic appliances?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.915,
            0.367,
